## Why This Is Asked
Addresses multi-cloud data governance, tenancy, and compliance through policy-as-code, ensuring data privacy, residency, and auditable CI validation in production-scale ML platforms.

## Key Concepts
- Data masking in logs/telemetry
- Per-tenant data residency and envelope encryption
- Tenant-aware RBAC across clouds
- Policy-as-code (OPA/Kyverno) + CI gates

## Code Example
```javascript
function redactPII(logEntry) {
  const redacted = { ...logEntry };
  for (const k of Object.keys(redacted)) {
    if (k.toLowerCase().includes('ssn') || k.toLowerCase().includes('email')) {
      redacted[k] = 'REDACTED';
    }
  }
  return redacted;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test fail-closed masking in CI across multiple tenants?
- What metrics would you surface to detect residency violations at runtime?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical design for tamper-resistant security data collection across heterogeneous Kubernetes estates, addressing post-breach forensics, automation, and resilience.

## Key Concepts

- Tamper-evident logs, audit policy, etcd encryption
- Immutable storage, HMAC signing, key rotation
- Secure log forwarding (webhooks, TLS)
- Runtime security (Falco) and IR playbooks
- Non-repudiation, data retention, failure modes

## Code Example

```javascript
function signEvent(event, key) {
  const crypto = require('crypto');
  const h = crypto.createHmac('sha256', key);
  h.update(event);
  return h.digest('hex');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test integrity guarantees across region failures?
- What are failure modes if the webhook sink is compromised?
